  "raw": {
    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/instructor-of-accounting-fairbanks-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor of Accounting",
      "description": "Instructor of Accounting - Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Instructor of Accounting Instructor of Accounting 533348 Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus UNAC Grade 40 UAF College of Business & Security Add to favorites View favorites Are you an experienced accountant or CPA? Do you enjoy sharing your knowledge with others? Please consider applying to teach as a term instructor at the College of Business and Security Management. We have amazing students who are eager to learn, and a team of dedicated and professional faculty and staff to provide support. A successful candidate will have outstanding teaching and communication skills. They will have demonstrated the potential to maintain their academic qualifications through scholarship and professional development, and will actively participate in departmental and university service. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates are required to possess an earned Master of Accountancy or related degree. Candidates should also have practical accounting experience. CPA preferred. Position Details: This position is located on the Troth Yeddha' campus in Fairbanks, starting in the Fall 2027 semester. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position complete with both a competitive salary and a full employee benefits package . UA provides a generous compensation package that includes retirement options, annual leave, 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental, and vision care coverage. New hires will be placed on the UNAC Faculty Salary Schedule , UNAC Grade 40, based on education and experience. Application review will begin on December 1st, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive priority consideration; however, the recruitment will remain open until filled. ☎️If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact Jim Wolverton, CBSM HR Coordinator, at jwolvert@alaska.edu or (907) 474-7461. *To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction.  Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. This position is represented by United Academics (UNAC). https://unitedacademicsak.org/ This position is term-funded and is reviewed annually for contract renewal at the University's discretion. The University of Alaska (UA) is responsible for providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities throughout the applicant screening process. If you need assistance in completing this application or during any phase of the interview process, please contact the ADA team at ua-ada@alaska.edu . The University of Alaska ( www.alaska.edu ) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution.  The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination ( www.alaska.edu/nondiscrimination ) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. The successful applicant is required to complete a background check. Any offer of employment is contingent on the background check. Your application for employment with the University of Alaska is subject to public disclosure under the Alaska Public Records Act. All employees at the University of Alaska are expected to uphold the highest standards of ethics and professionalism when conducting or engaged in university business. * Each university within the University of Alaska system publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in On-Campus Student Housing Facilities; in Noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.  The report also contains fire statistics for any fires occurring in an On-Campus Student Housing Facility during the three most recent calendar years. Access to the reports is available at: UAA : (Addresses Anchorage campus, Aviation Technology Complex, JBER - Elmendorf Extension, JBER - Richardson Extension, Kenai Peninsula College - Kachemak Bay campus, Kenai Peninsula College - Kenai River campus, Kodiak College, Kodiak High School Extension, Matanuska-Susitna College, Prince William Sound College, and Prince William Sound College - Cordova Extension) Online: https://www.uaa.alaska.edu/students/safety . Request a paper copy in person: UAA Police Department Office at Room 114 of Eugene Short Hall on the Anchorage campus / UAA Dean of Students Office at Room 122 of Rasmuson Hall on the Anchorage campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-786-1120 or police@uaa.alaska.edu / 907-786-1214 or uaa_deanofstudents@alaska.edu . UAF: (Addresses Fairbanks Campus, Bristol Bay Campus, Chukchi Campus, Community and Technical College, Kasitsna Bay Campus, Seward Marine Center, Tok Campus, Kuskokwim Campus, and Northwest Campus) Online: https://www.uaf.edu/orca/files/ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: UAF Office of Rights, Compliance and Accountability on the 3rd Floor of Constitution Hall. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-474-7300 or uaf-orca@alaska.edu . UAS: (Addresses the Juneau Auke Bay Campus, Juneau Technical Education Center, Sitka Campus, & Ketchikan Campus) Online: https://uas.alaska.edu/equity-and-compliance/docs/clery/UAS_ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: Hendrickson Building, Suite 202 on the Juneau campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-796-6371 or emailing uas.clery@alaska.edu . Apply Now Enter your First Name (required) 54d0fcce Enter your Last Name (required) 3350fa1c Enter your Email Address (required) 289513e1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Adjunct Faculty - Non-Credit (Course Development) Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Provost The College of Business and Security Management at the University of Alaska Fairbanks is looking for qualified adjunct faculty to create online course content and develop engaging curriculum for the following areas: Accounting, Applied Management, Business Administration, Economics, Homeland Security and Emergency Management, and Healthcare Management. Adjunct Faculty in Applied Management, Business Administration, Economics, and Healthcare Management Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Provost The College of Business and Security Management at the University of Alaska Fairbanks invites applications for adjunct instructors for the 2026-2027 Academic Year. This is a pooled position. Adjunct faculty teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses, dependent upon the needs of the organization. Strategy and Engagement Director - Alaska Critical Mineral Accelerator (ACMA) Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chancellor for Research The Director of Strategy & Engagement serves as the leader responsible for ACMA's Strategy, Engagement & Ecosystem Development functional area and is a member of the organization's leadership team. Reporting to the Chief Operating Officer, this position provides leadership in planning, developing, coordinating, implementing, and assessing ACMA's organizational strategy, strategic partnerships, ecosystem engagement, external alignment, and long-range organizational growth in support of the National Science Foundation Regional Innovation Engine.\n\nWorking across ACMA's mission-critical enterprise functions—Research & Development, Translation to Practice, and Workforce Development—the Director ensures organizational priorities, strategic partnerships, external investments, public policy engagement, and implementation activities remain aligned to achieve the objectives of the NSF Regional Innovation Engine Cooperative Agreement. The position serves as the primary leader responsible for strengthening Alaska's regional innovation ecosystem by cultivating strategic relationships among industry, Alaska Native Corporations, Tribal organizations, investors, universities, government agencies, entrepreneurial support organizations, and other partners essential to the Engine's long-term success and sustainability.\n\nThe Director of Strategy & Engagement leads a cross-cutting organizational function that integrates ACMA's long-range strategy, strategic partnerships, ecosystem development, stakeholder engagement, and implementation across a statewide regional innovation ecosystem. Government engagement is conducted in coordination with appropriate University of Alaska government relations offices and institutional leadership, consistent with University policy and delegated authority. The Director advises ACMA leadership on strategic opportunities, policy developments, funding strategies, partnership priorities, organizational alignment, and long-term growth. The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
