    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-ecosystem-ecology-fairbanks-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Ecosystem Ecology",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Ecosystem Ecology - Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor of Ecosystem Ecology Assistant or Associate Professor of Ecosystem Ecology 533534 Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus UNAC Grade 30 UAF College of Nat Science & Math Add to favorites View favorites The Institute of Arctic Biology and the Department of Biology and Wildlife at the University of Alaska Fairbanks invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position in terrestrial ecosystem ecology relevant to boreal forest ecosystems. This is a 9-month (full-time) tenure-track faculty position with a 3-month appointment extension supported by external funding (if available). The position duties will consist of 40% teaching, 50% research and 10% service. The rank of hire is open to Assistant or Associate Professor, commensurate with experience and leadership interest. Candidates should have expertise in terrestrial ecology, including fire ecology, isotope ecology, modelling, plant physiological ecology, or northern peatlands, with an interest in researching the boreal forest. We are interested in candidates who are integrative with their research, collaborative, and work in research teams. Candidates who are interested in engaging with the leadership of the Bonanza Creek Long-Term Ecological Research program are especially encouraged to apply. The position will be jointly appointed with the Department of Biology and Wildlife in the College of Natural Science and Mathematics and the Institute of Arctic Biology. The successful candidate will initially teach two courses per year in the Department of Biology and Wildlife, build and sustain a ongoing, externally-funded research program through the Institute of Arctic Biology involving mentorship of graduate and undergraduate students, and provide service to the university, profession, and general public. To thrive in this position, the successful candidate will excel in balancing teaching, research, and service. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the curricula of Biology and Wildlife Department’s Biological Sciences and Wildlife Biology programs through excellence and innovation in teaching across undergraduate and graduate levels, in-person and online courses. We seek candidates who can teach in general ecology, ecosystem ecology, areas of ecology related to specialized expertise, and courses that incorporate undergraduate research experiences. For research, the successful candidate will be expected to maintain an externally funded research program addressing ecologically relevant topics, especially those related to boreal forest ecosystems and of relevance for the Bonanza Creek Long-Term Ecological Research program. The successful candidate will contribute to service to the department and institute, the university, their profession, and the public. Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Biological Sciences or related field. Postdoctoral experience is preferred, but not required. To be considered for an Associate rank, the applicant must have experience commensurate with 5 years of experience as an Assistant or Associate Professor. *To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction.  Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are NOT eligible. Position Details: This position is located on the Troth Yeddha’ campus in Fairbanks, AK. This is a full-time, 9-month base appointment, FLSA exempt faculty position complete with a competitive salary and full employee benefits package . UA provides a generous compensation package that includes retirement options, annual leave, 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental and vision care coverage. New hires will be offered a competitive salary based on education and experience. Application review will begin on November 9, 2026. Applications received prior to this date will receive priority consideration; however, the recruitment will remain open until filled. *Finalists invited to an on-campus interview/visit will be required to give a research presentation during the visit. Feedback from faculty, staff and students will be considered. REQUIRED application documents: -Cover Letter -Resume or Curriculum Vitae -Teaching philosophy, experience and interests statement (1-2 pages) -Research Statement including experience, research agenda and how your research will be relevant to Alaska (1-2 pages) **Combine the Teaching and Research statements into a single document for upload ☎️If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact Sheri Hall, CNSM HR Manager, at sahall5@alaska.edu or (907) 474-6714 This position is represented by United Academics-AAUP/AFT (UNAC). https://www.unitedacademicsak.org The University of Alaska (UA) is responsible for providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities throughout the applicant screening process. If you need assistance in completing this application or during any phase of the interview process, please contact the ADA team at ua-ada@alaska.edu . The University of Alaska ( www.alaska.edu ) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution.  The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination ( www.alaska.edu/nondiscrimination ) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. The successful applicant is required to complete a background check. Any offer of employment is contingent on the background check. Your application for employment with the University of Alaska is subject to public disclosure under the Alaska Public Records Act. All employees at the University of Alaska are expected to uphold the highest standards of ethics and professionalism when conducting or engaged in university business. * Each university within the University of Alaska system publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in On-Campus Student Housing Facilities; in Noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.  The report also contains fire statistics for any fires occurring in an On-Campus Student Housing Facility during the three most recent calendar years. Access to the reports is available at: UAA : (Addresses Anchorage campus, Aviation Technology Complex, JBER - Elmendorf Extension, JBER - Richardson Extension, Kenai Peninsula College - Kachemak Bay campus, Kenai Peninsula College - Kenai River campus, Kodiak College, Kodiak High School Extension, Matanuska-Susitna College, Prince William Sound College, and Prince William Sound College - Cordova Extension) Online: https://www.uaa.alaska.edu/students/safety . Request a paper copy in person: UAA Police Department Office at Room 114 of Eugene Short Hall on the Anchorage campus / UAA Dean of Students Office at Room 122 of Rasmuson Hall on the Anchorage campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-786-1120 or police@uaa.alaska.edu / 907-786-1214 or uaa_deanofstudents@alaska.edu . UAF: (Addresses Fairbanks Campus, Bristol Bay Campus, Chukchi Campus, Community and Technical College, Kasitsna Bay Campus, Seward Marine Center, Tok Campus, Kuskokwim Campus, and Northwest Campus) Online: https://www.uaf.edu/orca/files/ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: UAF Office of Rights, Compliance and Accountability on the 3rd Floor of Constitution Hall. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-474-7300 or uaf-orca@alaska.edu . UAS: (Addresses the Juneau Auke Bay Campus, Juneau Technical Education Center, Sitka Campus, & Ketchikan Campus) Online: https://uas.alaska.edu/equity-and-compliance/docs/clery/UAS_ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: Hendrickson Building, Suite 202 on the Juneau campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-796-6371 or emailing uas.clery@alaska.edu . Recommended Jobs Data Center Technician Fairbanks, Alaska, United States SW Office of Information Technology The Data Center Operations (DCO) group within the University of Alaska’s Office of Information Technology (OIT) is seeking a full-time Data Center Technician. The successful candidate will monitor the status of the UA’s statewide computer network, enterprise applications, hosted computer systems, and data center infrastructure, resolving or escalating any issues as needed. The Data Center Technician on duty maintains security of the state-of-the-art data center, monitors the building’s CCTV system, provides After Hours Service Desk support, and performs hardware installations. The successful candidate will be able to work shiftwork and overtime in a 24x7x365 data center, and must be comfortable working independently as part of a team. Current availability is for a swing-shift position, 4:00 pm - midnight. The option of moving to a different shift in the future would be based on seniority. Program Administrator Coordinator Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chancellor for Research The Program Administrative Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for the Center for Transformative Research in Metabolism (TRiM), with the primary objective of reducing administrative burden on the Principal Investigator, Scientific Program Manager, Research Project Leaders, and other scientific personnel. The Coordinator maintains the organizational infrastructure required for a complex, multi-investigator NIH-funded Center and ensures that meetings, documentation, reporting, deadlines, communications, and follow-up activities occur efficiently and reliably. Executive Assistant to the Director Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chancellor for Research The Institute of Arctic Biology  (IAB) at the University of Alaska Fairbanks is seeking an organized, collaborative, and detail-oriented Executive Assistant to the Director. This position provides high-level administrative support to the Director, serves as the primary point of contact for IAB, manages the IAB Director’s Office, and coordinates IAB communications and events.  Join a dynamic team dedicated to IAB’s mission to advance research and innovation for healthy Arctic communities and ecosystems. The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/post-doctoral-fellow-nsf-critical-mineral-engine-fairbanks-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Fellow - NSF Critical Mineral Engine - Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Post Doctoral Fellow - NSF Critical Mineral Engine Post Doctoral Fellow - NSF Critical Mineral Engine 533602 Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus Grade 50 UNAC Post Doctoral Fellow UAF Geophysical Institute Add to favorites View favorites The Geophysical Institute is a research-focused organization at the University of Alaska Fairbanks. The university offers a competitive work environment with strong benefits, including retirement and health insurance, generous leave policies, and tuition waivers for UAF courses. The Geophysical Institute values collaboration, accountability, and the exchange of ideas. We foster a professional and respectful environment dedicated to serving Alaska through applied science. Career growth and professional development are supported and encouraged. As a public, regional, comprehensive university, UAF welcomes applications from individuals with a wide range of backgrounds and experiences. The Postdoctoral Researcher will advance applied research for the NSF Critical Mineral Accelerator Engine in Alaska, working with university, industry, and community partners to address barriers across the critical minerals value chain. The position will help translate research into practical technologies, partnerships, and economic opportunities for Alaska. This position is funded through the NSF Engines: Critical Mineral Accelerator Engine in Alaska, supported by the U.S. The National Science Foundation. The aim of this fellowship is to assist Dr. Sean Regan and Dr. Florian Hofmann in the study of critical mineral fingerprinting using U-Pb-TREE analysis from modern river catchments in Alaska. The immediate study will focus on characterizing detrital zircon from streams draining variably mineralized catchments and developing chemical proxies to assess mineral prospectivity. This will include the development of innovative methodology and theory that isolates specific petrogenetic processes specific to mineralization. However, other research questions will also be pursued, including optimization of newly installed instrumentation for U-Pb-TREE analysis, including the development of routines, alternative mineral phases, and applications. Fellows will be encouraged to pursue their own research questions as well. To thrive in this role, the Postdoctoral Researcher will bring scientific curiosity, sound research judgment, and a collaborative approach to working with industry and university partners. They will be comfortable pursuing rigorous research while keeping practical applications and Alaska’s economic opportunities in view. Minimum Qualifications: PhD in geology, geophysics, geological engineering, materials science, mineral processing, or a closely related field relevant to the assigned research. The degree must be completed by the time of appointment. Position Details: This position is full-time, term-funded, exempt, 9 + 3-month position complete with a competitive salary and UA employee benefits package. UA provides a generous compensation package that includes retirement options, annual leave, 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental, and vision care coverage. Please attach a resume, cover letter, and the names and contact information of three (3) professional references with your application. *This position will be physically located at the UAF campus in Fairbanks, Alaska. The successful finalist will be expected to report to duty at the UAF office on the first day of employment. We review applications on a rolling basis. Because we may close the posting once a sufficient pool of qualified candidates is established, we encourage early submission. Please note that once a viable pool is identified, further applications may not be reviewed To be eligible for this position, applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction. Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. If you need assistance applying to this posting, please contact GI - Office of Human Resources at 907-474-7357 or at uaf-gi-hr@alaska.edu . This position is represented by United Academics (UNAC). http://www.unitedacademics.net/ This position is term-funded and is reviewed annually for contract renewal at the University's discretion. The University of Alaska (UA) is responsible for providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities throughout the applicant screening process. If you need assistance in completing this application or during any phase of the interview process, please contact the ADA team at ua-ada@alaska.edu. The University of Alaska ( www.alaska.edu ) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution.  The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination ( www.alaska.edu/nondiscrimination ) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. The successful applicant is required to complete a background check. Any offer of employment is contingent on the background check. Your application for employment with the University of Alaska is subject to public disclosure under the Alaska Public Records Act. * Each university within the University of Alaska system publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report which contains information regarding campus safety and security including topics such as: campus law enforcement authority; crime reporting policies; campus alerts (Timely Warnings and Emergency Notifications); fire safety policies and procedures; programs to prevent dating violence, domestic violence, sexual assault and stalking; the procedures the University will follow when one of these crimes is reported; and other matters of importance related to security on campus. The report also contains information about crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in On-Campus Student Housing Facilities; in Noncampus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University or a recognized student organization; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.  The report also contains fire statistics for any fires occurring in an On-Campus Student Housing Facility during the three most recent calendar years. Access to the reports is available at: UAA : (Addresses Anchorage campus, Aviation Technology Complex, JBER - Elmendorf Extension, JBER - Richardson Extension, Kenai Peninsula College - Kachemak Bay campus, Kenai Peninsula College - Kenai River campus, Kodiak College, Kodiak High School Extension, Matanuska-Susitna College, Prince William Sound College, and Prince William Sound College - Cordova Extension) Online: https://www.uaa.alaska.edu/students/safety . Request a paper copy in person: UAA Police Department Office at Room 114 of Eugene Short Hall on the Anchorage campus / UAA Dean of Students Office at Room 122 of Rasmuson Hall on the Anchorage campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-786-1120 or police@uaa.alaska.edu / 907-786-1214 or uaa_deanofstudents@alaska.edu . UAF: (Addresses Fairbanks Campus, Bristol Bay Campus, Chukchi Campus, Community and Technical College, Kasitsna Bay Campus, Seward Marine Center, Tok Campus, Kuskokwim Campus, and Northwest Campus) Online: https://www.uaf.edu/orca/files/ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: UAF Office of Rights, Compliance and Accountability on the 3rd Floor of Constitution Hall. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-474-7300 or uaf-orca@alaska.edu . UAS: (Addresses the Juneau Auke Bay Campus, Juneau Technical Education Center, Sitka Campus, & Ketchikan Campus) Online: https://uas.alaska.edu/equity-and-compliance/docs/clery/UAS_ASFSR.pdf . Request a paper copy in person: Hendrickson Building, Suite 202 on the Juneau campus. Request a paper copy by mail: 907-796-6371 or emailing uas.clery@alaska.edu . Recommended Jobs Physical Access Control Systems Assistant Manager Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Vice Chancellor for Admin. Services We’re looking for a motivated, detail-oriented, and adaptable Assistant Access Control Systems Manager to join our team! Accounts Receivable Specialist Anchorage, Alaska, United States UAA VC Administrative Services The Office of the Bursar at the University of Alaska Anchorage (UAA) invites applications for the position of Accounts Receivable Specialist. As a key member of our student‑facing team, you will play an essential role in managing current and past‑due student accounts and coordinating third‑party sponsorships. The Office of the Bursar oversees all university receipts and is committed to providing excellent customer service to students and external sponsors alike. If you have a passion for service, a strong eye for detail, and a desire to help students navigate the financial side of their college experience, this could be the perfect role for you. UAF Events Coordinator Fairbanks, Alaska, United States UAF Chancellor * The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    }
